Subject: Slims the JS-to-JS call frame record

What this does
  Slims the JS-to-JS call frame record.

Why we need it
  A record frame carried several fields nothing in the register VM reads (`rt`, the transfer form's `set_d`/`set_s` whose `regvm_t_move_xfer_slow` handler no longer exists, and `func_obj`, a duplicate of `sf->cur_func`); `rec->ctx` is read only by the register-file consistency checker and `sf->cur_sp` is never read for a record frame.

What it adds
  `regvm_record_fill`, the entry-record setup and the in-loop rebind drop the corresponding stores (the struct shrinks by four members); `rec->ctx`/`run.ctx` are compiled only under `QJS_REGVM_RCCHECK`; the one `func_obj` reader, `init_ctor`'s `super` path, now reads `f->sf->cur_func`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
